Excalibur is much better than most think in my very biased
opinion.

> The only weapon better than Excalibur in *every* situation is
> Grayswandir.

In every *combat* situation *when* it exists.  Excalibur can exist
for a lawful character much earlier in the game and that matters
a lot for players not skilled in early survival.  Also there are an
assortment of non-combat advantages to Excalibur only offset
by Grayswandir's hallucination resistance.

> Snickersnee does almost as much damage without annoying
> named demons ... it's a close call between the two.

To me that's an advantage that only applies a small fraction of
the time.  While exploring Gen if I land in a level and telepathy
tells my there's a named demon on the level, I will want to switch
to a weapon other than Excalibur.  By then I'll have at least one
very good alternative.

> The two *brands
> (while strong) are both specialists and turn to garbage when you need
> them most (Gehennom with Firebrand.  Astral and foo-liches with
> Frosty.  Dealing with hostile Archons for both.)

Both smash potions.  Generally bad but for some players good.

Excalibur searches - Almost always good.  Even if sightless
monsters can see you most of them are either weak or slow and
it has no effect on sighted monsters in line of sight until you are
permanently invisible.

Excalibur resists level drain - Rarely needed but never a rarely a
negative.

Excalibur's damage may not be doubled, but it does apply to
*every* hit.  That means one of the double damage artifacts
needs to be well enchanted before it gets better than Excalibur.
So will I switch from Excalibur to Grayswandir?  As soon as
Grayswandir is +3 or better yes.  Will I switch from Excalibur
to Frost Brand?  As soon as Frosty is +3 or better probably.
Will I switch from Excalibur to Firey?  Very tough call I say.

The primary time I think Excalibur loses its appeal is on the
way back up with the Amulet.  By then the one artifact I want
the most is Magicbane anyways and not because of its combat
strength.



